Reasoning: use dynamicDarkColorScheme on Android 12+, fall back to a custom scheme. Apply at the theme root and let components consume colorScheme roles.

``kotlin
@Composable
fun AppTheme(dark: Boolean = true, content: @Composable () -> Unit) {
  val ctx = LocalContext.current
  val scheme = if (Build.VERSION.SDK_INT >= 31) {
    if (dark) dynamicDarkColorScheme(ctx) else dynamicLightColorScheme(ctx)
  } else {
    if (dark) darkColorScheme(primary = Color(0xFFD0BCFF)) else lightColorScheme()
  }
  MaterialTheme(colorScheme = scheme, typography = Typography(), content = content)
}
``

Rules: use MaterialTheme.colorScheme.* (surface, surfaceContainer, primaryContainer, outline) instead of hardcoded colors; request no permission; dynamic color is per-user wallpaper.
